  "body": "## What changed\n\n`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_robust.rs`: once the robust lathe axis fit settles, its inlier band shrinks from 3% of the bar's radius (0.3 mm on r10) to 4× the kept facets' median miss, with a floor of 1e-9 × the radius, and the line is refitted. This repeats while the band keeps shrinking.\n\n- Facets of a true cylinder, cone or end face meet the axis exactly, so they stay in. A cross hole's mouth ring and its floor strip sit near the axis plane but not in it, so they drop out.\n- Every tightened refit must pass the same checks as before, including the full judgement over all facets. A refit that fails isn't taken, and the last trusted fit stands. A fit that can't be trusted is still refused by name.\n- An exact revolve keeps its plain fit bit for bit. The spindle law's 0.0005 mm is untouched.\n- `tests/punched_bar`: #117's mirror-hole workaround is removed. The helper that merges duplicates and joins opposite holes stays, renamed `merged`.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `lathe_cross_drill::a_bar_with_one_modelled_cross_hole_fits_on_the_spindle_and_drills_clean`: an r10 bar with one modelled cross hole and no mirror reads exact (worst about 3e-17 mm) and the cross drill posts clean. It **fails on main** (worst 0.00088 mm, over 0.0005).\n- `axis_robust::a_near_meridian_strip_is_set_aside_by_the_tightened_band`: **fails on main** (offset 3.3e-4 mm).\n- `axis_robust::a_rectangular_prism_is_still_refused_as_not_revolved`: guards against regression.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Cross-drill suites green without the mirrors: drilling_cross_box, _spindle, _stock, drill_reach, drill_reach_fit, lathe_cross_drill 5, drilling_cross, _part, _rapids.\n- lathe_spindle_* green; motion lib 128 plus the multiaxis, rotary and turning suites green; clippy on motion and app is clean.\n- Only red: the 7 known #159 lathe tests, which fail the same on main and are fixed in PR #135.\n- Not fixed by this change: #113 (a 90° keyway still fails the plain fit's 90% check before the robust pass) and #152 (the short-bar isotropy check).\n\nChangelog: Lathe axis fit tightens its inlier band to the revolve's own noise, so a round bar with one modelled cross hole reads its true axis within the spindle tolerance and cross-drills clean\n\nFixes #116\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
